<%# locals: (epic_slug:) %>
<%#
  The EPIC CHIP — the one piece of connective tissue between an epic and its
  tasks on the board (devops-v3-design.md section 3). Rendered beside the
  task-slug chip on every card whose task carries `tasks.epic_slug`; renders
  NOTHING when the task belongs to no epic, so a card never carries an empty
  slot. Clicking it filters the board to that epic (/tasks?epic=<slug>), which
  the deployments board honours too.

  Its own partial, deliberately small: the card partial is shared with an
  in-flight operator-windows change that will seat a countdown BESIDE this
  chip, and two chips in one row are easier to merge than one row rewritten
  twice. Keep the chip's markup here; keep the row it sits in over there.

  Colour is the primary role's tint (theme tokens, right in both themes), so
  the chip reads as a different KIND of handle from the mono task slug next to
  it.
  Server-rendered conditionally, so no Alpine display gating is needed.
%>
<% epic_slug = local_assigns.fetch(:epic_slug).to_s %>
<% if epic_slug.present? %>
  <a href="<%= tasks_path(epic: epic_slug) %>"
     data-test="task-epic-chip"
     data-epic="<%= epic_slug %>"
     title="Epic <%= epic_slug %> — show only this epic's tasks"
     class="inline-flex items-center shrink-0 max-w-[9rem] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-3xs font-semibold leading-none truncate transition <%= status_tone(:primary) %> hover:bg-primary/20"><%= epic_slug %></a>
<% end %>
